      "text_raw": "The equivalent input noise\nvoltage due to the two resis-\ntors is given in this slide.\nThe voltage noise of resis-\ntor R appears directly in\n1\nseries with the output. The\nnoise of the other resistor R\n2\nis transformed towards the\noutput by the resistor ratio\nand factor n. Its contribution\nto the output is a lot larger\nthan that of resistor R .\n1\nActually, the noise of R\n2\nis amplified to the output\nwhereas the noise of R is\n1\nnot.\nHow can the output noise then be minimized?",
      "text": "The equivalent input noise voltage due to the two resistors is given in this slide. The voltage noise of resistor R appears directly in 1 series with the output. The noise of the other resistor R 2 is transformed towards the output by the resistor ratio and factor n. Its contribution to the output is a lot larger than that of resistor R . 1 Actually, the noise of R 2 is amplified to the output whereas the noise of R is 1 not. How can the output noise then be minimized?"
